# Three recommended essays and two reserves

**October 31, 2026.** The AI coordinator recommends **E050, E009 and E012**, with **E078 and E041** in reserve, after reading all ten frozen manuscripts and their twenty accepted independent Codex Astra / ultra audits. The lists are not a numerical ranking. The earlier 60/40 selection remains a separate completed stage.

| Place | Essay and surviving contribution | Main limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary | [E050 · What Holding Cannot Tell Us About Letting Go](../essays/selection-20261018/E050.md): identical limiting outcomes under permanent interventions can conceal opposite release outcomes; one staged release works throughout the specified family from the stated initial condition. | The equation family and time scale must be independently justified. Hidden dynamics and robust control already have close predecessors. |
| Primary | [E009 · Before You Tell Us to Try Again](../essays/selection-20261018/E009.md): when a decision is justified by later correction, the entire correction route must survive the very harm that might require it. | This is a conditional development of known ideas about revisability; the threshold of sufficient protection remains open. |
| Primary | [E012 · When a Remedy Becomes Evidence](../essays/selection-20261018/E012.md): destroying evidence can leave a duty to help against a later error even after payment and accurate communication, if that destruction still impairs a protected defence. | Substitute duties and replacement-proof costs are established. The specific later application remains the possible contribution, with two cited full texts inaccessible. |
| Reserve | [E078 · Revocable Consent and the Cost of Preserving Choice](../essays/selection-20261018/E078.md): keeping refusal genuinely possible may require paying for an unused fallback, with different cost allocation for unilateral and shared changes. | Fair starting rights, mixed changes and excessive costs need further justification. |
| Reserve | [E041 · What Foreknowledge Can Take Away](../essays/selection-20261018/E041.md): a spoiler can remove the experience of correcting one's own reasonable interpretation, even if the informed encounter is better overall. | Earlier work already discusses reinterpretation; the narrower combination and its aesthetic value remain contestable. |

The choice favours a clearly identified additional result and a developed explanation of its limits. It does not certify historical priority or make the normative premises of E009 and E012 uncontroversial. [All ten reasons and reopening conditions](../evidence/deep-verification/20261031/coordinator/CONTRIBUTION_MATRIX.json) explain why F02, F06, E055, E079 and E074 were not selected. E055's close ER-018 comparator reports a publication date after our exact October 19 version; the earlier 2000 and 2021 overlaps remain independently relevant.

Before submission, add the newly identified close predecessors and sharpen positioning through recorded AI revisions, then check the changed claims. Prepare anonymous manuscripts and a methodology report, confirm the submission account and current form requirements, and obtain an explicit submission instruction. These frozen versions were not rewritten or submitted during verification.

